node_modules
*.local

# Never ship local environment files to a Vercel build.
#
# `vercel --prod` uploads the working directory and builds it on Vercel, and
# the CLI's built-in ignore list covers `.env.local` / `.env.*.local` but not a
# plain `.env`. Nitro then loads whatever `.env` it finds into `process.env` at
# build time (see nitro/vite: `.env`, `.env.local`, `.env.<mode>`), so a local
# `.env` pointing at 127.0.0.1 can end up baked into a production build. The
# real values belong in the Vercel project's environment variables.
.env
.env.*
